<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 140 mln stg late help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 140 mln stg late help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with around 140 million stg of unspecified late assistance.</p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    200 MLN    200 MLN    350 MLN    350 MLN</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    =	    =	    151 MLN    291 MLN</p>
<p> DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS   =	    =	     51 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BAND 2  BANK BILLS   =	    =	    100 MLN*   =</p>
<p> UNSPECIFIED LATE ASSISTANCE     =		=	 140 MLN</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-15/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
